      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of 342:**\n   \\[\n   342 \\div 2 = 171 \\quad (\\text{since 342 is even})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   171 \\div 3 = 57 \\quad (\\text{since the sum of the digits of 171 is } 1+7+1 = 9, \\text{ which is divisible by 3})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   57 \\div 3 = 19 \\quad (\\text{since the sum of the digits of 57 is } 5+7 = 12, \\text{ which is divisible by 3})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   19 \\div 19 = 1 \\quad (\\text{since 19 is a prime number})\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n   \\[\n   342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the prime factorization of 285:**\n   \\[\n   285 \\div 3 = 95 \\quad (\\text{since the sum of the digits of 285 is } 2+8+5 = 15, \\text{ which is divisible by 3})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   95 \\div 5 = 19 \\quad (\\text{since the sum of the digits of 95 is } 9+5 = 14, \\text{ which is not divisible by 3})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   19 \\div 19 = 1 \\quad (\\text{since 19 is a prime number})\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n   \\[\n   285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n   \\]\n\n3. **Identify the common factors of 342 and 285:**\n   From the prime factorizations, we see that both numbers share the prime factors 3 and 19. Therefore, the common prime factors are:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Common factors} = 3 \\times 19 = 57\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the largest common factor:**\n   The largest common factor is 57.\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
