      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of 342:**\n   - Divide 342 by the smallest prime number, which is 2:\n     \\[\n     342 \\div 2 = 171\n     \\]\n   - Now, factorize 171. Divide 171 by 3:\n     \\[\n     171 \\div 3 = 57\n     \\]\n   - Factorize 57 by 3:\n     \\[\n     57 \\div 3 = 19\n     \\]\n   - 19 is a prime number. Therefore, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n     \\[\n     342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n2. **Find the prime factorization of 285:**\n   - Divide 285 by the smallest prime number, which is 3:\n     \\[\n     285 \\div 3 = 95\n     \\]\n   - Now, factorize 95. Divide 95 by 5:\n     \\[\n     95 \\div 5 = 19\n     \\]\n   - 19 is a prime number. Therefore, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n     \\[\n     285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n3. **Identify the common factors:**\n   - The prime factorization of 342 is \\(2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\\).\n   - The prime factorization of 285 is \\(3 \\times 5 \\times 19\\).\n   - The common prime factors of 342 and 285 are 3 and 19.\n   - Therefore, the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285 is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{GCD} = 3 \\times 19 = 57\n     \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
