      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of these two numbers. Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of 342 and 285.\n\nThe prime factorization of 342:\n\\[\n342 \\div 2 = 171\n\\]\n\\[\n171 \\div 3 = 57\n\\]\n\\[\n57 \\div 3 = 19\n\\]\n\\[\n19 \\div 19 = 1\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[\n342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nThe prime factorization of 285:\n\\[\n285 \\div 3 = 95\n\\]\n\\[\n95 \\div 5 = 19\n\\]\n\\[\n19 \\div 19 = 1\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[\n285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nNext, we identify the common prime factors of 342 and 285. The common prime factors are 3 and 19. The GCD is found by taking the lowest power of these common prime factors:\n\\[\n\\text{GCD} = 3^1 \\times 19^1 = 3 \\times 19 = 57\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{57}\n\\]",
